# Pellerex-owned paths — every PR touching these waits on review from the
# Pellerex operator account. Referenced as a user handle (not a team) so the
# same line works both here in the scaffold repo (pellerex-platform org) and
# in every tenant repo after clone. The operator is a member of every org
# Pellerex creates, so the reference resolves everywhere. Tenants remain free
# to change everything else (application source, tests, docs, app config)
# without Pellerex approval.
#
# What's guarded and why:
# - infrastructure/         Helm charts, K8s manifests, secret provider classes.
# - .github/workflows/      CI/CD pipeline callers — swapping the reusable
#                           workflow reference would bypass the Pellerex deploy
#                           chain even if infrastructure/ is untouched.
# - .github/CODEOWNERS      Self-guard so this file can't be removed in a
#                           single PR to disable the whole guard.
# - Dockerfile              Contract with the Helm chart — port, entrypoint,
#                           runtime shape. If tenants change it, the platform
#                           deploy assumptions break.
# - .dockerignore           Controls what enters the image and thus what runs
#                           in the cluster.
/infrastructure/         @pellerex-tech
/.github/workflows/      @pellerex-tech
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @pellerex-tech
/Dockerfile              @pellerex-tech
/.dockerignore           @pellerex-tech
